        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(a) Employees involuntarily terminated due to layoff will have the termination payment schedule, as well as the method of payment computed in accordance with the appropriate collective bargaining agreement. In addition, regular full-time and regular part-time employees (not term or temporary employees) who have been involuntarily terminated pursuant to the force adjustment procedures of the applicable collective bargaining agreement and have a minimum of one (1) year net credited service as of the date of termination are eligible for up to $2,500 in funds for certain education, training, outplacement and relocation expenses. These funds will be available through the Funds for the Alliance/ETOP Distribution (FAED) program.",
